abstract: >-
  AL-MIZAN is a complete quantum emulator implemented in pure Python with zero external dependencies,
  unifying state vector simulation (up to 16 qubits), density matrix evolution (up to 8 qubits),
  Steane [[7,1,3]] quantum error correction, zero-noise extrapolation (Richardson), and pedagogical
  GDSII layout generation. It provides sealed SHA-256 mathematical certificates for bounded verifications:
  Point Square Conjecture (PC-1..PC-6 verified by exhaustion on the declared finite domain), Turing theorem on the Riemann strip <= 100
  (29 zeros certified via interval arithmetic), and BSD verification on named elliptic curves.
  Strict honesty constraints: every artifact carries its computational bound, no open millennium problem
  is claimed as solved. Developed by M. Ahmed EL BAHLOUL under the IMAM8MAHDI initiative.
